# Denylist, not an allowlist: with `COPY *.mjs` in the Dockerfile, any `!`
# re-include pattern makes BuildKit walk every directory to look for matches —
# including data/certbot/conf/accounts, which certbot creates root-only, so the
# build dies with "permission denied" on the Pi. A plain exclude of data/ is
# never descended into.
#
# Keep secrets (.env, data/: certbot keys, the sqlite cache) out of the build
# context; the rest is just weight the Dockerfile never COPYs.
data
.env
deploy.env
node_modules
*.test.mjs
ansible
nginx
fail2ban
